  "question": {
    "text": "The temperature of an ideal gas is increased from $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ to $127^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, then percentage increase in $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}$\r\n\r\nis"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$37 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$11 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$33 \\%$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$15.5 \\%$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know, $\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{mms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{RT}}{\\mathrm{M}}}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\%$ increase in\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{R} \\mathrm{T}_{2}}{\\mathrm{M}}}-\\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{RT}_{1}}{\\mathrm{M}}}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{RT}_{1}}{\\mathrm{M}}}} \\times 100 \\\\\r\n\r\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{T}_{2}}-\\sqrt{\\mathrm{T}_{1}}}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{T}_{1}}} \\times 100 \\\\\r\n\r\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{400}-\\sqrt{300}}{\\sqrt{300}} \\times 100 \\\\\r\n\r\n=\\frac{20-17.32}{17.32} \\times 100=15.5 \\%\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
